      <VULN>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIGRef</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>VMware vSphere 6.7 RhttpProxy Security Technical Implementation Guide :: v1r3</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-240722</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>medium</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-APP-000176-WSR-000096</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-240722r879613_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>VCRP-67-000007</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>The rhttpproxy private key file must be protected from unauthorized access.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>The rhttpproxy's private key is used to prove the identity of the server to clients and securely exchange the shared secret key used to encrypt communications between the web server and clients.

By gaining access to the private key, an attacker can pretend to be an authorized server and decrypt the TLS traffic between a client and the web server.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>At the command prompt, execute the following command:

# stat -c "%n permissions are %a, is owned by %U and group owned by %G" /etc/vmware-rhttpproxy/ssl/rui.key

Expected result:

/etc/vmware-rhttpproxy/ssl/rui.key permissions are 600, is owned by root and group owned by root

If the output does not match the expected result, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content_Ref</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>C-43955r679677_chk</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>At the command prompt, execute the following commands:

# chmod 600 /etc/vmware-rhttpproxy/ssl/rui.key
# chown root:root /etc/vmware-rhttpproxy/ssl/rui.key</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
